  - [1mImplicit by involvement[0m — you created it, you're assigned it, or you've edited it. Zero effort, matches how most
    trackers behave, but can get noisy and needs an assignee field in the model from the start.
  - [1mBoth, with implicit defaults[0m — involvement auto-subscribes you, and you can explicitly mute or watch to override.
    Most flexible; needs a stored subscription record per task-user pair rather than a derived answer.

  I lean toward [1mboth with implicit defaults[0m, because the failure mode of pure explicit watching is silence — you miss
  the thing you cared about most because you never starred it. But for a single-user local app it's also the most
  machinery, so the simpler option is defensible.

